WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.436
-Two centrist Democrats
are blocking

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:04.770
the entire Democratic agenda

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.773
without saying
what they actually want,

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:09.308
essentially threatening to
detonate Joe Biden's presidency.

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:12.312
Meanwhile, Fox News
is trying unsuccessfully

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.080
to make all
the super popular stuff

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.316
in Biden's agenda sound scary.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.851
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:22.154 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:23.356
It's hard to overstate

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.124
the stakes of
what's happening right now --

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:27.360
basically the entire
Democratic agenda,

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.928
the policies Joe Biden ran on

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.563
and promised voters
he would pass

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.631
are on the line
in negotiations over

00:00:32.631 --> 00:00:35.635
the $3.5 trillion
reconciliation bill.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.436
And you can tell
how high the stakes are

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:40.206
from this shot of
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.608
at the annual congressional
baseball game last night.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.043
-We have our first
pinch hitter of the day.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:47.480
It was Rodney Davis
at the top of the lineup.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.349
-Speaker no doubt
happy about that play,

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.818
but she is known
as a big sports fan

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.586
and often after dealing

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:56.288
with a lot of really
difficult reporter questions

00:00:56.288 --> 00:00:58.591
related to what's going on,
she'll say,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.927
"Oh, I stayed up
and watched the game last night

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:03.029
and I didn't get to bed
at a good time."

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:06.399
And then there she is at
7:00 or 8:00 in the morning,

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:09.269
back at work, so...

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.804
That's true for members
of both parties.

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:14.407
It's amazing
what all of them do.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.342
-Pelosi's working the phones
like the Mets

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.810
just hired her as a scout.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.545
[ As Nancy Pelosi ]
"You're going to love this guy.

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:23.082
60 years old,
throws in the mid-to-low 40s,

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:24.817
and we can get him
for league minimum.

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:28.421
Yeah, I think we found
our new deGrom."

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.023
But Pelosi had to work the phone
instead of watching

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:35.194
what I'm sure
was a terrible baseball game.

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:36.763
You think
regular baseball is slow?

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.564
Imagine what it's like
with these bozos.

00:01:38.564 --> 00:01:40.399
Nancy Pelosi looking to make
a pitching change,

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:42.835
but not sure she has the votes,
which means they're going to

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:45.471
make the hot dogs race
around the outfield yet again.

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:49.808
And oh, no.
One of the hot dogs is dead.

00:01:49.808 --> 00:01:51.210
That's how high the stakes are.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.345
Democrats need to deliver
on the promises they made,

00:01:53.345 --> 00:01:56.282
not just to avoid the political
consequences of failure,

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.618
which would be massive, but also
to improve people's lives.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.887
Now, I could tell you about

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.788
all the good
this bill would do myself,

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:05.657
or you could just listen
to a Fox News host

00:02:05.657 --> 00:02:07.092
try to make it sound bad.

00:02:07.092 --> 00:02:10.029
-Free universal
pre-kindergarten.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:12.231
Free community college.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:14.867
Free 12 weeks of family leave.

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:17.870
They want to extend
the temporary child care credit

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.173
with additional taxpayer
subsidies for the rest of time.

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:23.142
This is really considered
a foot in the door

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:26.745
for a minimum annual income that
the government would pay people.

00:02:26.745 --> 00:02:28.715
Think about where
we're going with all this.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:29.916
They want to expand Medicare

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.718
to include
dental, vision, and hearing

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:35.255
and lower the age from 65 to 60.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:37.356
What else does this bill do?

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:41.560
It funds the Green New Deal,
retrofitting buildings,

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.296
subsidizing solar, wind,

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.631
environmental justice
and environmental equity,

00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:47.633
whatever the hell that means.

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:49.769
Electric government vehicles.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.904
They want to subsidize
low-income housing.

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:53.706
Gee, that's never
been tried before.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:58.344
They want to create sustainable
housing, public transportation.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.146
-If you want to know
who Republicans are,

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:01.948
just look at
what horrifies them.

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:04.116
"They want sustainable
housing, these monsters!

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:06.052
And yet not one penny
in the bill

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:09.022
for an army of Terminator robots
at the border!

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.690
They're never going
to learn to hurt us!"

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.659
He's talking about
free education for children

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:15.261
with the same level
of feigned outrage

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:18.063
as Nicole Kidman finding out her
husband just murdered someone.

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:19.432
He should be walking through
Central Park

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.534
at 2:00 a.m. in a $5,000 coat.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.236
[ As Nicole Kidman] "My husband,
the mysterious British doctor

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:25.605
who won't tell me
about his childhood,

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.406
vanished in the middle
of the night."

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:29.675
"Oh, okay, he probably
murdered someone."

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:31.510
"He said he's at
a medical convention."

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.112
"Okay, but I think
he murdered someone."

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:35.882
"I found this bloody butcher
knife hidden behind a rock.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.216
Maybe it's from a surgery."

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:39.185
"Do you have someplace
you can stay tonight?"

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:41.421
Fox host Brian Kilmeade
tried the same thing this week

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.455
in an interview with
Republican Senator John Kennedy.

00:03:43.455 --> 00:03:46.525
Kilmeade was trying
to ask Kennedy what Republicans

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:49.596
would do about the fact
that the Democrats' agenda

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:51.363
is likely to be popular
with voters

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:55.334
and came so close to realizing
what he was actually admitting.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.503
-Senator, here's
what I fear, though.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.205
If you tell someone,
I'm giving you a free preschool,

00:04:00.205 --> 00:04:03.376
if you tell someone, I'm giving
you free junior college,

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:06.212
if you tell someone, I'm going
to give you free school lunch,

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:08.447
if you tell someone
free elder care --

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:10.249
Issues need to be addressed,
yes,

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:11.984
but if you write
all those people a check,

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:14.286
you've got their votes,
and we're sitting there

00:04:14.286 --> 00:04:15.988
and have to balance the books.

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:17.457
Doesn't that worry you?

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.258
-He's like the one employee
at IKEA

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:21.027
who's worried that giving out
free meatballs

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.128
will attract more customers.

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:23.262
"Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:24.564
If we give these out,
aren't more people

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:25.665
just going to come to the store?

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:27.100
Okay.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.869
Just don't come to me when
we run out of Fjallbo shelves."

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:31.937
The point is,
polling has repeatedly shown

00:04:31.937 --> 00:04:33.839
that these policies
are popular with voters.

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:35.841
They're a big reason
Democrats won the White House

00:04:35.841 --> 00:04:37.977
and two Senate seats
in Georgia runoffs

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:39.645
that gave them
full control of Congress.

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:43.016
But now two centrist Democrats
backed by corporate interests,

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:44.684
whether it's fossil fuels
or big pharma,

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.419
are essentially threatening
to blow all that up,

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:47.587
and they won't even say why.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.988
Just name something in this bill
you don't like --

00:04:49.988 --> 00:04:52.157
universal pre-K,
expanded Medicare benefits,

00:04:52.157 --> 00:04:53.426
child care subsidies.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.594
You don't think people
want help with child care?

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:58.130
I think if you polled parents
who were stuck at home

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.465
with their kids
for the last year

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:02.434
if they're in favor
of expanded child care programs,

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:04.804
the results would be 75% "yes,"

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.473
25% "my soul has been crushed
into a fine powder

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:10.276
and I no longer have the ability
to respond to pollsters."

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:12.278
As a parent who was stuck at
home with my kids all year --

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:14.012
and, by the way,
extremely privileged

00:05:14.012 --> 00:05:16.115
to even have that option --
let me just say,

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.785
I will sign my life over
to any politician

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:21.387
who makes it easier to get them
the hell out of the house.

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.423
I'm so desperate for
a few minutes of quiet,

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:25.257
I started taking them
to the only daycare

00:05:25.257 --> 00:05:26.793
I could find with any openings,

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:30.629
and it was called Igor's House
of Knives and Broken Glass.

00:05:30.629 --> 00:05:33.566
They have a great Russian
language immersion program.

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.101
My kids can already
say things like,

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.535
[ Speaking in Russian ]

00:05:36.535 --> 00:05:37.670
which is "careful, glass" and

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.072
[ Speaking in Russian ]

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:41.107
which is, "he has a knife."

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:44.944
Yet Sinema will not tell anyone
what she wants or doesn't want.

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:47.747
In fact, progressives
have been openly begging her

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:50.750
to tell them what she wants, as
Congressman Ro Khanna explains.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.684
-I've never seen her
do an interview.

00:05:52.684 --> 00:05:54.920
It's like an oracle, an enigma.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.589
I mean, she never comes
on television.

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.324
She never answers journalism.

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:02.227
-What has she said that she
wants, as far as you know?

00:06:02.227 --> 00:06:03.562
-That's the question.

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:05.798
The president keeps begging her,
"Tell us what you want.

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:08.300
Put a proposal forward."

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.635
I have no idea what she wants.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.570
I don't think her colleagues
know what she wants.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.839
I don't think the president
knows what she wants.

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:16.342
I don't think House moderates
knows what she wants.

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:19.178
We've said, "Let's get in
a room. Let's negotiate.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:21.079
Let's come up with a deal."

00:06:21.079 --> 00:06:23.582
And I just don't understand it.

00:06:23.582 --> 00:06:25.484
-She made three trips
to the White House Tuesday,

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.019
and people still don't know
what she wants.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:29.021
This is like the time
I took my grandmother

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.189
to The Cheesecake Factory.

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:31.590
Really, Nana?

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:33.158
You can't find anything?

00:06:33.158 --> 00:06:34.960
Because the menu's
a [bleep] book.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.263
Oh, watch my language,
she says.

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:39.064
Like I haven't seen
her play bridge.

00:06:39.064 --> 00:06:40.099
I mean, seriously,
Kyrsten Sinema.

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:41.200
What are you doing?

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.335
Everyone wants to know,
what do you want?

00:06:43.335 --> 00:06:44.537
Explain yourself.

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:46.138
You're not LeBron.
This isn't "The Decision."

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:47.607
You don't get
to keep it a secret

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:49.976
until you announce it live
on ESPN with Jim Gray.

00:06:49.976 --> 00:06:51.644
And by the way, this routine

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:53.346
isn't helping
Sinema politically, either.

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:56.582
A recent poll found that
about 56% of Democrats

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.384
in the state
Ms. Sinema favorably,

00:06:58.384 --> 00:06:59.552
compared with 80%

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:01.254
for Senator Mark Kelly,
a fellow Democrat.

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:03.856
People are sick
of these weird mind games.

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:05.724
You have the right
to an opinion,

00:07:05.724 --> 00:07:06.893
but the people who elected you

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:08.661
have a right to hear
what that opinion is.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:11.297
You're a United States senator.
You don't get to play coy.

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:13.632
No one likes coy anyway,
especially in politics.

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:16.002
It's not your job
to be mysterious.

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:17.369
This isn't a perfume commercial.

00:07:17.369 --> 00:07:18.638
No one's like, "Oh,

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:20.472
I hope she comes out
from behind her folding fan

00:07:20.472 --> 00:07:21.974
and tells us her secret."

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:24.543
People are just annoyed,
like Congresswoman Katie Porter,

00:07:24.543 --> 00:07:27.045
who had this to say last night
about Manchin and Sinema.

00:07:27.045 --> 00:07:29.448
-If they have concerns,
if they have problems,

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:30.716
tell us what they are,

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:35.287
but we simply
can't negotiate with ourselves

00:07:35.287 --> 00:07:37.856
and away from what
the American people want

00:07:37.856 --> 00:07:41.560
if there are no meaningful
competing concerns.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:44.163
I was elected to represent
the people of Orange County

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:47.099
and to fight for families, to
stand up to corporate interests.

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:50.403
I was not elected to read
the mind of Kyrsten Sinema.

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:52.972
Thank goodness, because I have
no idea what she's thinking.

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:54.106
-Oh man, you better watch out.

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:55.274
If you piss off Katie Porter,

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:57.310
you might get
the white board treatment.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.278
Biden and Porter
aren't the only ones mystified

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:00.912
by what Manchin and Sinema
are doing.

00:08:00.912 --> 00:08:03.682
After Manchin issued yet another
grandstanding statement

00:08:03.682 --> 00:08:05.484
last night proclaiming
that he could not support

00:08:05.484 --> 00:08:07.053
spending
trillions of dollars,

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:10.156
again, without explaining what
specifically he was against,

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:11.690
Senate Budget Chairman
Bernie Sanders

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.160
expressed his frustration
to reporters, saying,

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.195
"Look, you can talk
to Mr. Manchin.

00:08:16.195 --> 00:08:18.931
I can't speak for Mr. Manchin.
I'm not a psychologist."

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:20.500
Although I wish he were,

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:21.967
because I think
he'd be great at it.

00:08:21.967 --> 00:08:25.270
Bernie seems like he'd be
a tough love kind of therapist.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.706
[ As Bernie Sanders ] "Oh, you
have a fear of intimacy?

00:08:27.706 --> 00:08:29.542
Well, that's the first time
I've ever heard that one.

00:08:29.542 --> 00:08:30.976
Let me write that one down.

00:08:30.976 --> 00:08:34.680
What a new phenomenon.
You're really special.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.181
I'm gonna write you
a prescription

00:08:36.181 --> 00:08:38.150
for one teddy bear."

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:41.287
And yet Sinema
continues to engage in this

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:44.657
maddening little shtick where
she refuses to explain herself

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:46.292
or make any specific requests.

00:08:46.292 --> 00:08:48.527
Yesterday, a reporter
finally caught up with her

00:08:48.527 --> 00:08:51.296
and tried to ask her
to respond to progressives

00:08:51.296 --> 00:08:53.899
who are frustrated with
her unwillingness to negotiate,

00:08:53.899 --> 00:08:55.835
and she basically
played word games.

00:08:55.835 --> 00:08:58.504
-What do you say to progressives
that are frustrated

00:08:58.504 --> 00:08:59.838
that they don't know
where you are?

00:08:59.838 --> 00:09:01.407
-I'm in the Senate.

00:09:01.407 --> 00:09:02.641
-There are progressives
within the Senate

00:09:02.641 --> 00:09:03.742
that are frustrated that

00:09:03.742 --> 00:09:05.076
they don't know where you are,
either.

00:09:05.076 --> 00:09:07.847
-I'm, like, clearly
right in front of the elevator.

00:09:07.847 --> 00:09:09.714
-Ah, what fun.
A little wordplay.

00:09:09.714 --> 00:09:11.483
This is Congress,
not vaudeville.

00:09:11.483 --> 00:09:13.586
No one's interested
in your Abbott &amp; Costello act.

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:15.887
Not even Bernie.
He saw them live.

00:09:15.887 --> 00:09:19.524
His review is even
quoted on the poster.

00:09:19.524 --> 00:09:21.761
You guys are risking blowing up
the Biden presidency

00:09:21.761 --> 00:09:23.395
and handing power back
to a movement

00:09:23.395 --> 00:09:25.731
led by an insane person
who's spent the last year

00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:27.866
trying to unravel
American democracy

00:09:27.866 --> 00:09:29.335
and will absolutely
follow through

00:09:29.335 --> 00:09:30.770
next time he gets the chance.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:33.672
One of his lawyers wrote an
instruction manual for a coup.

00:09:33.672 --> 00:09:35.374
One of his cronies
at the Justice Department

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:36.976
had a plan
to overthrow the election,

00:09:36.976 --> 00:09:39.377
and on top of that, Trump keeps
going around the country,

00:09:39.377 --> 00:09:40.646
confessing to new crimes.

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:42.548
Like the time he told
a rally crowd

00:09:42.548 --> 00:09:44.116
he tried to bully
the governor of Georgia

00:09:44.116 --> 00:09:45.851
into overturning
his state's results.

00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:48.453
-Sure, we spoke
to Governor Kemp.

00:09:48.453 --> 00:09:51.290
Sure, he will not do anything
on election integrity.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:53.792
I said, "No, you're kidding.
Just call him again.

00:09:53.792 --> 00:09:57.429
You know, I mean, maybe
he never got the message."

00:09:57.429 --> 00:10:00.832
They come back the next day,
"Sir,

00:10:00.832 --> 00:10:03.568
Governor Kemp won't do anything
on election integrity."

00:10:03.568 --> 00:10:06.305
Remember, we wanted to call
a special election

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:07.673
so that we could go
-- Marjorie --

00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:11.109
so we could go into
election integrity?

00:10:11.109 --> 00:10:12.744
What is wrong with that?

00:10:12.744 --> 00:10:13.946
So when these guys,

00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:15.848
they're young and nice guys,
they came back,

00:10:15.848 --> 00:10:16.982
they said,
"He won't do it, sir."

00:10:16.982 --> 00:10:19.784
I said, "Let me handle it.
This is easy."

00:10:19.784 --> 00:10:21.820
You know,
I got this guy elected.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:24.923
One thing has
nothing to do with the other.

00:10:24.923 --> 00:10:27.526
One thing has nothing --
there's no quid pro quo.

00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:29.028
I said,
"Brian, listen, you know,

00:10:29.028 --> 00:10:33.132
you have a big election
integrity problem in Georgia.

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:36.268
I hope you can help us out
and call a special election,

00:10:36.268 --> 00:10:37.636
and let's get to
the bottom of it

00:10:37.636 --> 00:10:39.138
for the good of the country.

00:10:39.138 --> 00:10:41.974
Let's get to the bottom of it
for the good of your state.

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:44.876
Let's go, election integrity.
What could be better than that?"

00:10:44.876 --> 00:10:47.279
"Sir, I'm sorry.
I cannot do that."

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:48.714
I said, "Whoa."

00:10:48.714 --> 00:10:50.649
-Why does he scream
the word "integrity"

00:10:50.649 --> 00:10:51.850
like George Costanza?

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:53.152
"Integrity, Jerry!

00:10:53.152 --> 00:10:54.686
They said
I don't have integrity!"

00:10:54.686 --> 00:10:56.522
"You think you have integrity?"

00:10:56.522 --> 00:10:58.424
"Oh, I got integrity, baby.

00:10:58.424 --> 00:11:00.526
I got integrity up the wazoo."

00:11:00.526 --> 00:11:02.427
Also, it looks like
the "sir" stories are back,

00:11:02.427 --> 00:11:03.695
which are even
more ridiculous now

00:11:03.695 --> 00:11:05.164
that he's no longer president.

00:11:05.164 --> 00:11:08.300
He's just a retiree shanking
drives at his golf course.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.969
"They came to me, tears pouring
out of their eyes

00:11:10.969 --> 00:11:13.872
and they said, 'Sir,
that was a beautiful shot, sir.

00:11:13.872 --> 00:11:16.108
That honking
from the parking lot

00:11:16.108 --> 00:11:19.444
was probably about
something else, sir.

00:11:19.444 --> 00:11:22.314
Here's a hernia pillow for
your golf cart, sir.

00:11:22.314 --> 00:11:24.516
Inflated
to your specifications, sir.'"

00:11:24.516 --> 00:11:27.519
Trump and his cultists on Fox
are trying to make things

00:11:27.519 --> 00:11:29.488
like universal pre-K
and sustainable housing

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:30.790
sound scary because in reality,

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.791
they know those items
are popular with voters,

00:11:32.791 --> 00:11:35.527
and even they will
inadvertently admit that.

00:11:35.527 --> 00:11:37.663
That's why Democrats need to get
on with passing their agenda

00:11:37.663 --> 00:11:40.198
and why Manchin and Sinema
need to get out of the way.

00:11:40.198 --> 00:11:42.300
Not only will it do a lot
of good for a lot of people,

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:43.535
it will in large part determine

00:11:43.535 --> 00:11:44.937
the course of
Joe Biden's presidency.

00:11:44.937 --> 00:11:47.339
If they fail, they could
very well hand power back

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:48.407
to Trump and the GOP.

00:11:48.407 --> 00:11:50.075
If they succeed,
then voters will at least

00:11:50.075 --> 00:11:52.511
have reason to believe them
when they say they have --

00:11:52.511 --> 00:11:54.146
-Integrity!

00:11:54.146 --> 00:11:55.914
-This has been A Closer Look.

